    {
      "id": "the-merchant-of-venice/sceneII_22.9/p@72741",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [
        "drama"
      ],
      "text": "MESSENGER.\nMadam, there is alighted at your gate\nA young Venetian, one that comes before\nTo signify th’ approaching of his lord,\nFrom whom he bringeth sensible regreets;\nTo wit (besides commends and courteous breath)\nGifts of rich value; yet I have not seen\nSo likely an ambassador of love.\nA day in April never came so sweet,\nTo show how costly summer was at hand,\nAs this fore-spurrer comes before his lord.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
